<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tūtēlāris</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		tutela (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			(Acc. to tutela, I. B.) <i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to guardianship</i>, <i>tutelar</i>,
				<i>tutelary</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					12, 3, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">instrumenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					27, 7, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 24 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praetor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. M. Aur. 19 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Acc. to tutela, II. A.) Di, <i>tutelar deities</i> of
			places, <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 3, 9</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Arn. 3, 114</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
